{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"valign","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLValign","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLValign","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLValignO"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to the MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"code":"valign","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" attribute.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/valign","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/valign"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome"]]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"The valign attribute is used to indicate vertical alignment to the top, middle, bottom, or baseline of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"text. Defaults are implementation-dependent.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"property","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLMetronomeV6valignAA9MXLValignOSgvp","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","role":"symbol","title":"valign","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"valign","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLValign","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLValignO"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/valign":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/valign","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/valign","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The valign attribute is used to indicate vertical alignment to the top, middle, bottom, or baseline of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"text. Defaults are implementation-dependent."}],"title":"valign","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"valign"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLValignO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLValign"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLValign":{"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLValign","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLValign","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The valign type is used to indicate vertical alignment to the top, middle, bottom, or baseline of the text. If"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the text is on multiple lines, baseline alignment refers to the baseline of the lowest line of text. Defaults"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are implementation-dependent."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLValign","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlvalign","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLValign","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The metronome type represents metronome marks and other metric relationships. The beat-unit group and per-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"minute element specify regular metronome marks. The metronome-note and metronome-relation elements allow for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the specification of metric modulations and other metric relationships, such as swing tempo marks where two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"eighths are equated to a quarter note \/ eighth note triplet. Tied notes can be represented in both types of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"metronome marks by using the beat-unit-tied and metronome-tied elements. The parentheses attribute indicates"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whether or not to put the metronome mark in parentheses; its value is no if not specified. The print-object"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute is set to no in cases where the metronome element represents a relationship or range that is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"displayed in the music notation."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMetronome"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLMetronome","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMetronome"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"}}}